Look up libc's gettimeofday, not glibc's __gettimeofday, on QNX.

datefudge's gettimeofday() calls __gettimeofday(), which finds the real
function with dlsym(RTLD_NEXT, "__gettimeofday") -- glibc's internal alias.
QNX's libc exports only gettimeofday, so the lookup returns NULL and every
program that calls gettimeofday() under datefudge jumps to address 0. On
QNX the next definition after the preloaded library is libc's
gettimeofday itself.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/datefudge.c
+++ b/datefudge.c
@@ -69,7 +69,12 @@
     int res;
 
     if(!libc_gettimeofday)
+#ifdef __QNX__
+        /* QNX's libc has no __gettimeofday: the next gettimeofday is libc's. */
+        libc_gettimeofday = (typeof(libc_gettimeofday))dlsym (RTLD_NEXT, "gettimeofday");
+#else
         libc_gettimeofday = (typeof(libc_gettimeofday))dlsym (RTLD_NEXT, __func__);
+#endif
     res = (*libc_gettimeofday)(x,y);
     if(res) return res;
     set_fudge(&x->tv_sec);
